# Flutter Code Quality

- Keep business rules out of widgets.
- Do not duplicate API contracts in multiple places.
- Prefer explicit models and mappers over dynamic JSON manipulation throughout the app.
- Remove dead code and unused dependencies.
- Keep comments focused on non-obvious decisions and invariants.
- Update `/flutter/docs/**` when architecture or behavior changes materially.
- New features must include the necessary loading/error/offline/sync states.
- Do not bypass analyzer/test failures to complete a feature.
